---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/") ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Residential Interior Design GTA | NV Studio Design"
  description="Residential interior design for houses across the GTA and Ontario. Space planning, materials, built-ins, kitchens, and bathrooms &mdash; developed alongside the architecture."
  keywords="residential interior design Toronto, GTA interior designer, kitchen design Toronto, home interior design Ontario"
>
  <section id="one">
    <div class="inner">
      <header class="major">
        <h1>Residential Interior Design</h1>
      </header>

      <p>
        Interiors are half of what a house feels like. We design them
        alongside the architecture &mdash; or as a standalone project when
        the shell is already there &mdash; for homes across the Greater
        Toronto Area and Ontario.
      </p>

      <h2>What&rsquo;s in scope</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Space planning and flow.</strong> How the rooms connect,
          how people move through them, and where the sight-lines land.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Kitchens and bathrooms.</strong> Layout, millwork,
          appliances, plumbing fixtures, and the services behind them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Built-ins and millwork.</strong> Cabinetry, wardrobes,
          wall units, and the detail drawings your fabricator needs.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Materials and finishes.</strong> Floors, tile, stone,
          paint, hardware &mdash; picked against real samples, not
          Pinterest.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Lighting.</strong> A layered plan &mdash; ambient, task,
          and accent &mdash; coordinated with the electrical rough-in.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>FF&amp;E guidance.</strong> Furniture and fixtures to the
          level of detail each client wants, from a shopping list to a
          complete specification.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Architecture and interiors, developed together</h2>
      <p>
        When we&rsquo;re doing both on the same project, the interior is
        part of the plan from day one. That means the kitchen island fits
        the structure, the bathroom doesn&rsquo;t hit the roof slope, and
        lighting circuits follow the joists without chasing them later.
      </p>
      <p>
        It&rsquo;s not glamorous work, but it&rsquo;s the difference between
        a house that photographs well on day one and a house that still
        works five years in.
      </p>

      <h2>Interior-only projects</h2>
      <p>
        Not every client needs new architecture. We also take on
        interior-only projects: kitchen renovations, principal-suite
        reworks, and full interior refreshes where the house envelope
        stays put and the rooms inside get rebuilt.
      </p>

      <h2>Selected interior work</h2>
      <div class="row gtr-50 gtr-uniform">
        <div class="col-4 col-12-medium">
          <article class="project-card">
            <a href={`${baseUrl}project-contemporary-kitchen-design`} class="image">
              <img
                src="images/projects/contemporary-kitchen-design/4-5-mxB1570PnXh3MKp8.jpg"
                alt="Contemporary kitchen design with premium finishes by NV Studio Design, GTA"
              />
            </a>
            <header class="major">
              <h3><a href={`${baseUrl}project-contemporary-kitchen-design`}>Contemporary Kitchen Design</a></h3>
              <p>Kitchen renovation</p>
            </header>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="col-4 col-12-medium">
          <article class="project-card">
            <a href={`${baseUrl}project-luxury-home-renovation`} class="image">
              <img
                src="images/projects/luxury-home-renovation/3-A3QOoKVygoIkW0VX.jpg"
                alt="Interior of a luxury home renovation by NV Studio Design, GTA"
              />
            </a>
            <header class="major">
              <h3><a href={`${baseUrl}project-luxury-home-renovation`}>Luxury Home Renovation</a></h3>
              <p>Whole-house interior</p>
            </header>
          </article>
        </div>
        <div class="col-4 col-12-medium">
          <article class="project-card">
            <a href={`${baseUrl}project-modern-residential-villa`} class="image">
              <img
                src="images/projects/modern-residential-villa/1-m5KLpxQggBCWDKl6.jpg"
                alt="Modern residential villa interiors designed by NV Studio Design"
              />
            </a>
            <header class="major">
              <h3><a href={`${baseUrl}project-modern-residential-villa`}>Modern Residential Villa</a></h3>
              <p>Integrated architecture and interiors</p>
            </header>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ul class="actions">
        <li><a href={`${baseUrl}portfolio`} class="button">View full portfolio</a></li>
      </ul>

      <ul class="actions">
        <li><a href={`${baseUrl}contact`} class="button primary">Book a Consultation</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
